{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541577-clan-s-curse-nosferatu","id":1541577,"title":"Clan's Curse (Nosferatu)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-05T07:04:48-07:00","id":1541577,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Clan's Curse (Nosferatu)","content":"I'm probably overthinking it, but this is something that came to mind. The Nosferatu curse changes their form, but if I understand correctly they assume that the pattern is not random, but that this externalizes their inner beast. All vampires in VTM have it, but this clan have it exposed. Now, would there be a pattern? Like, a more violent person would have big hands and rougher skin, or a more greedy person would have a swollen body and develop pus sores. In the case of the Nosferatu, would the beast be their worst characteristics? Or if you're more pessimistic, what is the afflicted person really like? Ugly and monstrous. So I think that those who change little with the curse would be those who have fewer defects or who don't see themselves in such a bad light. I know it's convenience, but many of them take on the classic Nosferatu form, with a shrunken nose, pointy ears, dry skin and varying color, so these would be the &quot;normal&quot; Nosferatu, but it is mentioned that the appearance of the antediluvian resembles a blue jellyfish, so I wonder what happened to give this result. Have you ever imagined what form you would take if you became a Nosferatu?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T09:38:42-07:00","id":1541590,"title":"","content":"I think that my skin would be tightly drawn on my skeleton and I would look very frail as it seemed that any appearance of body fat would be gone as I'm slender irl and I would have bluish purple tint to my complexion. I wouldn't be hideously deformed but walking around people would be a excerise of makeup and heavy use of Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> In VTR I'd probably look normal but maybe give off the chill of the grave vibes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T13:16:23-07:00","id":1541600,"title":"","content":"I think some of the development of the Nosferatu has taken strange turns by this obsession on their monstrosity or being disgusting. To me, the reason the Nosferatu exist is to just to enable characters who look similar to the depictions of Max Schreck and Klaus Kinski because the 1922 and 1979 Nosferatu movies are so iconic. Both are bizarre and unattractive, but not especially repulsive or inhuman. Neither, of course, live in sewers or otherwise disgusting habitats (nor do any of the original Nosferatu NPCs in Chicago By Night). It is unfortunately ironic that the inspirations for the clan essentially cannot be depicted as belonging to that clan.<br /> <br /> I don't mind the decision that their look was deemed as revolting or monstrous (Timbrook's stylized depictions of the clan are much more monstrous than Schreck's or Kinski's characters), but Appearance Zero does not by itself mean a person automatically breaks the Masquerade. I don't mind players and STs having the option to make Nosferatu characters particularly ugly or disgusting, but I don't think it should be a requirement. I just think there should Nosferatu still able to be among humanity without the need for Mask of a Thousand Faces. Still Appearance Zero, but perhaps something approaching Fair Glabro. I know the game allows this with a 5 point Merit of Rugged Bad Looks, and perhaps we can imagine Count Orlok as having that, but I would prefer a situation in the reverse where more horrific variations are done with Flaws and players have some latitude on the Masquerade breaking of their appearance. Maybe the more human looking ones might still attract attention from hunters in the know, but limited interaction with humanity should not be a deal breaker.<br /> <br /> (Perhaps in the World of Darkness there should be a genetic disorder, &quot;Nosferatu syndrome&quot;, that makes a small minority of people particularly repellant when that get old. That way certain looks don't automatically attract hunters. It'd be like killing anyone who looks albino.)<br /> <br /> In games that I ST, I hold that there are several recognizable main phenotypes of the clan. Individual Nosferatu appearance can always vary, but in general there appears to be lineages.<br /> <br /> The main morphology is the classic &quot;Rat&quot; style of Timbrook's stylized drawings. A variant of that is the more human looking Nosferatu akin to the movies, they tend to appear as repellant older men and women so they are the &quot;Decrepit&quot; line. This also fits for traditional &quot;crone&quot; figures like Baba Yaga. The third is a more brutish line of &quot;Grendels&quot; as I hold in my setting that Beowulf's foe Grendel was in fact a Nosferatu vampire (as was his &quot;dam&quot;, his sire). Large monstrous hags like Black Annis fit here too. The fourth is similar to the &quot;Rat&quot; line except they are more batlike than ratlike (of course inspired by Batboy of the tabloids), so they're the &quot;Bat&quot; line. The fifth is a &quot;Scaled&quot; line where we get characters that look like they have scales on their skin, so anything from the alligator men of real freakshows to Killer Croc or more reptillian or piscine looks. These phenotypes are not evenly divided. The classic Rat look is well over half of the clan.<br /> <br /> If a player had a good idea of another archetypal look, I'd probably add it to my list of common phenotypes for the clan.<br /> <br /> For the most part, a specific lineage of vampires overwhelmingly look like a specific line so it's likely there were 5th generation Methusalehs who spawned their own line. However, there are always exceptions and although it's not typical, it's not rare. So Khalid in Chicago and his line tend towards the &quot;Rat&quot; look, but some individuals in that line might appear more like the Bat or Decrepit lines. That way I can always adjust an individual Nosferatu's appearance to what I need, and I provide players flexibility in their own appearance.<br /> <br /> It's also a storytelling tool as I can have Nosferatu quarrel over those who look differently from them, or distinguish one group of Nosferatu in a domain descended from one progenitor from another group descended from an &quot;unrelated&quot; one. Or distinguish how this one childe continues to look like his sire, but this other childe not only looks different, his childer and grand childer appear more like him and thus are somehow &quot;breeding true&quot; (until of course, they don't).<br /> <br /> I happen to like patterns like this in the setting where vampires of a certain line or more likely to have things in common. (I use that for certain Flaws and other methods too.) I prefer that than simply having every Nosferatu be unique in their looks. And it isn't necessarily based on the person herself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  typos 09-07-2024, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T15:22:39-07:00","id":1541607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541577-clan-s-curse-nosferatu?p=1541590#post1541590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that my skin would be tightly drawn on my skeleton and I would look very frail as it seemed that any appearance of body fat would be gone as I'm slender irl and I would have bluish purple tint to my complexion. I wouldn't be hideously deformed but walking around people would be a excerise of makeup and heavy use of Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> In VTR I'd probably look normal but maybe give off the chill of the grave vibes</div> </div> </div> </div>So you would look like Dove from night road? Just more purple?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T15:29:58-07:00","id":1541609,"title":"","content":"Yes more bluish purple as it would sell the image that I look like that I have one foot firmly in grave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T15:37:27-07:00","id":1541612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541577-clan-s-curse-nosferatu?p=1541600#post1541600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mind the decision that their look was deemed as revolting or monstrous (Timbrook's stylized depictions of the clan are much more monstrous than Schreck's or Kinski's characters), but Appearance Zero does not by itself mean a person automatically breaks the Masquerade. I don't mind players and STs having the option to make Nosferatu characters particularly ugly or disgusting, but I don't think it should be a requirement. I just think there should Nosferatu still able to be among humanity without the need for Mask of a Thousand Faces. Still Appearance Zero, but perhaps something approaching Fair Glabro. I know the game allows this with a 5 point Merit of Rugged Bad Looks, and perhaps we can imagine Count Orlok as having that, but I would prefer a situation in the reverse where more horrific variations are done with Flaws and players have some latitude on the Masquerade breaking of their appearance. Maybe the more human looking ones might still attract attention from hunters in the know, but limited interaction with humanity should not be a deal breaker.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am certainly understand this point of view, but I guess the Nosferatu culture revolves around too much in their apparence and the fact that they need hide themselves, also I guess their curse really seems like a curse like that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541577-clan-s-curse-nosferatu?p=1541600#post1541600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone in games that I ST, I hold that there are several recognizable main phenotypes of the clan. Individual Nosferatu appearance can always vary, but in general there appears to be lineages.<br /> <br /> The main morphology is the classic &quot;Rat&quot; style of Timbrook's stylized drawings. A variant of that is the more human looking Nosferatu akin to the movies, they tend to appear as repellant older men and women so they are the &quot;Decrepit&quot; line. This also fits for traditional &quot;crone&quot; figures like Baba Yaga. The third is a more brutish line of &quot;Grendels&quot; as I hold in my setting that Beowulf's foe Grendel was in fact a Nosferatu vampire (as was his &quot;dam&quot;, his sire). Large monstrous hags like Black Annis fit here too. The fourth is similar to the &quot;Rat&quot; line except they are more batlike than ratlike (of course inspired by Batboy of the tabloids), so they're the &quot;Bat&quot; line. The fifth is a &quot;Scaled&quot; line where we get characters that look like they have scales on their skin, so anything from the alligator men of real freakshows to Killer Croc or more reptillian or piscine looks. These phenotypes are not evenly divided. The classic Rat look is well over half of the clan.<br /> <br /> If a player had a good idea of another archetypal look, I'd probably add it to my list of common phenotypes for the clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if this could count as a archetypal, but I already &quot;saw&quot; the concept of a orcus Nosferatu, literally a pigman.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T20:43:06-07:00","id":1541632,"title":"","content":"I like to play with different notions of the Nosferatu curse and not have it just be simple physical disfigurement and I played with that notion in the Vampire The Requiem setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T03:09:28-07:00","id":1541638,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that there's no rime or reason behind their appearance. Some say it's a reflection of the Beast, others that it is your own faults made manifest, many that it is a sign of your lineage.<br /> <br /> All seem to happen from time to time, but ultimately all fail to really explain anything.<br /> <br /> But other than that, I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, I don't mind the turn for the monstrous it took in Masquerade, but I think the idea of automatic Masquerade break isn't the best, even if the option sure should exist. It's even bad design in comparison to other clan weaknesses, either far too punishing or completely bypassed by a clan power.<br /> <br /> Requiem did a better job in this regard. V5 too, although not as good as Requiem. The idea of a repulsive but still human monster, as if wearing their vices in their sleeve, should certainly be an option, if not the standard at least for elders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T12:39:18-07:00","id":1541658,"title":"","content":"I agree that the Nosferatu curse should have no rythme or reason but maybe common triats might appear in certain branches of the clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T14:23:46-07:00","id":1541700,"title":"","content":"I think that if the form that Nosferatu's body takes is related to him in some way, this ends up increasing the horror aspect, after all, the person is in a situation where he cannot hide or deny his flaws, after all, it is written on his face and since the curse does not break, this creates a whole trauma in his head that he can do whatever he wants, try anything until he is satisfied, at the end of the day this does not change who he is, a monster, the monster that he always was and will be until the day of his second death, others may think differently, but this does not change anything and he knows, because he remembers this every time he looks in the mirror and lets the mask fall. But I understand those who do not want to play with such a depressing concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T15:38:30-07:00","id":1541707,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> Comment made me have a crazy idea, what if the Nosferatu clan wasn't actually just another clan, but rather a collection of outcasts? There is a flaw, I can't remember the name now, but it makes kindreds from other clans manifest the curse of the Nosferatu, or something close to it, so each of the strains or sub-types of Nosferatu are actually lineages of other clans that manifested this problem, as if it were a genetic error in humans. The strains that look like animals are alternative lineages of the Gangrel or Ministry, the ones that look like corpses or mummies came from the Giovanni or Lasombra, the big ones possibly came from the Brujah, the ones that look more human came from the Toreador and the ones that look like classic Nosferatu would be the true Nosferatu, or maybe not, maybe they were part of another clan that was lost a long time ago.<br /> <br /> You can even go further if you want, for example: The Nosferatu of the cadaveric strain would be the result of a blood contamination caused by the constant use of disciplines related to Necromancy or Oblivion. The animalistic strains that have bat or scale skin traits, and even traits of other animals, would come as a result of Gangrels who consume a lot of blood from a specific animal and this &quot;contaminated&quot; their blood or could also have been born from a Tremere experiment, something similar to what happened with the gargoyles.<br /> <br /> I don't know if this could help spice up any chronicle, but it's something interesting to think about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T11:39:09-07:00","id":1541746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541577-clan-s-curse-nosferatu?p=1541700#post1541700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that if the form that Nosferatu's body takes is related to him in some way, this ends up increasing the horror aspect, after all, the person is in a situation where he cannot hide or deny his flaws, after all, it is written on his face and since the curse does not break, this creates a whole trauma in his head that he can do whatever he wants, try anything until he is satisfied, at the end of the day this does not change who he is, a monster, the monster that he always was and will be until the day of his second death, others may think differently, but this does not change anything and he knows, because he remembers this every time he looks in the mirror and lets the mask fall. But I understand those who do not want to play with such a depressing concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with this take is that when extended to a whole clan it seems... Hard to swallow.<br /> <br /> Either the clan as a whole is abnormally good at only Embracing people that are truly and irredeemably monsters at their core since before their Embrace, and in a particular way that makes them recognize a heavily symbolic and weirdly specific representation of their failings, or it isn't hard to conclude this take is full of shit.<br /> <br /> It does work for some. It is an interesting concept for a character, and there's likely a number of Nosferatu that do live like that. But it works best as a customized curse for a specific character than a general thing for an entire clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T14:56:55-07:00","id":1541752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541577-clan-s-curse-nosferatu?p=1541746#post1541746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with this take is that when extended to a whole clan it seems... Hard to swallow.<br /> <br /> Either the clan as a whole is abnormally good at only Embracing people that are truly and irredeemably monsters at their core since before their Embrace, and in a particular way that makes them recognize a heavily symbolic and weirdly specific representation of their failings, or it isn't hard to conclude this take is full of shit.<br /> <br /> It does work for some. It is an interesting concept for a character, and there's likely a number of Nosferatu that do live like that. But it works best as a customized curse for a specific character than a general thing for an entire clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree, it's not hard to think that everyone has flaws that can be seen more by the curse. I think you're thinking from the perspective that only truly despicable people would suffer and become monsters, however, that's not the idea, this appearance can appear in anyone and only in very rare cases would it express itself little and the kindred would seem normal, as if the curse said that humanity as a general rule is made up of horrible and imperfect people. Got it?<br /> <br /> By the way, I'm not expressing any personal point of view here, just explaining my interpretation, so don't take it too seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T17:32:02-07:00","id":1541757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541577-clan-s-curse-nosferatu?p=1541752#post1541752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to disagree, it's not hard to think that everyone has flaws that can be seen more by the curse. I think you're thinking from the perspective that only truly despicable people would suffer and become monsters, however, that's not the idea, this appearance can appear in anyone and only in very rare cases would it express itself little and the kindred would seem normal, as if the curse said that humanity as a general rule is made up of horrible and imperfect people. Got it?<br /> <br /> By the way, I'm not expressing any personal point of view here, just explaining my interpretation, so don't take it too seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not taking too seriously, just expressing my opinion on this trope in relation to the clan curse.<br /> <br /> The problem with your doing things like in your opening post is that you end up with a formulaic approach to their appearance that ends up limiting options, all the while making them easier to read in character. Imagine in Vampire society someone whose personality, even if just the worst part, is literally written in their faces.<br /> <br /> Characters may have this as a theory, and some may even be effective examples. In fact, all you need to have the kind of horror you described is that the actual character believe it. But to make it into an objective fact with observable effect has other effects on the game, and on other possible tropes.<br /> <br /> By the way, even if it is true, does the character believe it? You can't simply force the player to play their character as believing that their appearance reflects their inner flaws, even if this is objectively true in your game, and then you lose all that pathos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T06:28:40-07:00","id":1541777,"title":"","content":"I would never use this as a rule in the game, because players have the freedom to customize their character as they wish within the game's proposal and there are people who just go for the basics, so you know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}